WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
This is the brief on social media algorithms.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.000
You know, the video feeds on our phones aren't just showing us random clips.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.000
They actually use secret mathematical rules to control exactly what we see and, well, keep us hooked.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
First, we kind of have to ask why do these apps care so much about our attention?

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Well, it basically comes down to showing you more ads.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Platforms use algorithms to predict exactly what you'll like, share, or watch just to keep you scrolling.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Experts call this surveillance capitalism,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
which is making money off your tracked data.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
It's honestly like a rigged carnival game, specifically designed to keep you playing until you're totally out of tokens.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Second, to actually pull that off, they track your every move.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
I mean, every single pause, like, and swipe is being monitored.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
They use these manipulative tricks called dark patterns.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Think infinite scrolling or pushing super emotional videos to basically hack your brain's natural reactions.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
It's literally like having a tiny detective in your pocket

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
taking furious notes on your favorite snacks just to build an irresistible trap.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Finally, because these formulas instantly boost whatever gets the fastest reaction,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.000
they create microtrends.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.000
You know, massive fads that explode in days and vanish just as fast.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:16.000
By quietly curating our reality, the algorithm creates this huge illusion of choice.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
We think we're in the driver's seat of our own interests, but are we really?

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Thanks to these math rules, we're just passengers on a ride they built.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000
So the next time you fall down a scrolling rabbit hole, just remember,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.000
you aren't just watching the app.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.000
The app is watching you.